    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1060">

                <pb facs="0948" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.003/102.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-20T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 20, 1913—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>571. The Government has promulgated, under date of 18th, the following Executive
                    order raising the tariff:</p>
                <p>[Text of decree. It adds 50% to the duties provided in Articles 1 and 2 of the
                    tariff law.]</p>
                <p>This has been expected, but impression is very bad. Exchange 36.75.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
